{"description":"Provide per-driver, least-privilege credential injection so worker agent CLIs can authenticate WITHOUT the host env allow-list: a secrets broker that injects only the credential a given driver needs (model API keys, and scoped git auth for steward's own worktree operations), never `os.Environ()`, plus an egress policy so credentials cannot be exfiltrated to arbitrary hosts.","acceptanceCriteria":"A worker receives only the credentials its driver declares (test asserts no other secret is present).\nThe host env is never blanket-inherited; `GH_TOKEN`/`SSH_AUTH_SOCK`/cloud vars are not leaked to workers.\nAn egress policy restricts worker network to an allow-list (model endpoints; documented).\nSteward's own git remote ops authenticate via scoped, broker-provided credentials."}